Rollback point: save and restore VRAM pages, their super-sample flags and the CLUT on the GPU

DW5XL issue 049 draws extra pictures between two of the game's on the same GS and then puts the GS back exactly
as the game left it. GSInterface::rollback_save(pages) flushes and copies the given VRAM pages to a side buffer
with GPU buffer copies, in every slice the current sampling rate uses (single-rate, reference, samples), together
with each page's "may super sample" flag and the current CLUT instance. GSInterface::rollback_add(pages) keeps
more pages for the same point: the caller calls it just before a write behind the point reaches a page that is
not kept yet, so the page is kept as it is after everything submitted before that write (each batch in a side
buffer of its own). GSInterface::rollback_restore() flushes, copies the pages back, marks them as externally
written (cached textures of those pages are invalidated and the host copy is refreshed), restores the flags and
makes the saved CLUT a fresh instance (memoized palettes are dropped). If the sampling rate changed in between,
only the single-rate slice goes back. The register state is the caller's (get_register_state /
clobber_register_state).

A second GS memory (DW5XL issue 049, fact-finding 2026-11-11): GSInterface::copy_pages_from(source, pages)
copies pages of another GSInterface on the same device into this one's VRAM on the GPU (every slice in use,
each page's flag, the current CLUT), so extra pictures can be drawn apart from the game's GS.

Two GS memories drawing in turns (DW5XL issue 049, amendment v3.7): each keeps its own work open while the
other draws, so that where the turns fall does not show in a picture (what a render pass draws depends on where
it ends). Granite waits for every open command buffer of the device when a frame context ends, and
GSRenderer::flush_submit ends one. With GSInterface::set_frame_context_hold(hold) a flush leaves the frame
context alone while `hold` says true; the caller makes it say so while another GS memory of the device has open
command buffers (GSInterface::has_open_command_buffers). The frame context is only where the device frees
things.

Applies on top of 0001-0006.

